## Purpose and Rationale

Create a tracing Subscriber implementation that wraps another subscriber and adds rich formatting to stderr output. This bridges the Rust tracing ecosystem with rich_rust's beautiful output capabilities.

## Background

The Rust ecosystem standardizes on the `tracing` crate for structured logging. FastMCP already uses tracing throughout. Rather than replacing the logging infrastructure, we wrap it - intercepting events and routing them through our rich formatter while preserving all existing functionality.

## Technical Specification

### Architecture Decision

We use a **layered approach** rather than a custom Subscriber:

```rust
// crates/fastmcp-console/src/logging/subscriber.rs

use tracing_subscriber::{Layer, Registry, fmt};
use tracing_subscriber::layer::SubscriberExt;
use std::io::{self, Write};

/// A tracing Layer that formats output using rich_rust
pub struct RichLayer<W: Write = io::Stderr> {
    formatter: RichLogFormatter,
    writer: W,
    console: FastMcpConsole,
}

impl<S, W> Layer<S> for RichLayer<W>
where
    S: tracing::Subscriber + for<'lookup> tracing_subscriber::registry::LookupSpan<'lookup>,
    W: Write + 'static,
{
    fn on_event(&self, event: &tracing::Event<'_>, ctx: tracing_subscriber::layer::Context<'_, S>) {
        // Format the event
        let formatted = self.formatter.format_event(event);

        // Get span context for hierarchical display
        let spans = ctx.event_scope(event)
            .map(|scope| scope.from_root().collect::<Vec<_>>())
            .unwrap_or_default();

        // Render to stderr using rich console
        self.console.write_log(&formatted, &spans);
    }

    fn on_new_span(&self, attrs: &tracing::span::Attributes<'_>, id: &tracing::span::Id, ctx: tracing_subscriber::layer::Context<'_, S>) {
        // Optionally display span entry (configurable)
        if self.formatter.show_span_entry {
            // Format span entry notification
        }
    }
}
```

### Subscriber Builder

Provide ergonomic construction:

```rust
/// Builder for configuring the rich tracing subscriber
pub struct RichSubscriberBuilder {
    theme: Option<FastMcpTheme>,
    show_timestamps: bool,
    show_targets: bool,
    show_file_line: bool,
    show_span_entry: bool,
    level_filter: LevelFilter,
    stderr_writer: bool,
}

impl RichSubscriberBuilder {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            theme: None,
            show_timestamps: true,
            show_targets: true,
            show_file_line: false,
            show_span_entry: false,
            level_filter: LevelFilter::INFO,
            stderr_writer: true,
        }
    }

    pub fn with_theme(mut self, theme: FastMcpTheme) -> Self {
        self.theme = Some(theme);
        self
    }

    pub fn with_timestamps(mut self, show: bool) -> Self {
        self.show_timestamps = show;
        self
    }

    pub fn with_level_filter(mut self, filter: LevelFilter) -> Self {
        self.level_filter = filter;
        self
    }

    /// Build and install as global subscriber
    pub fn init(self) -> Result<(), SetGlobalDefaultError> {
        let subscriber = self.build();
        tracing::subscriber::set_global_default(subscriber)
    }

    /// Build without installing
    pub fn build(self) -> impl Subscriber {
        let context = DisplayContext::detect();
        let theme = self.theme.unwrap_or_default();
        let formatter = RichLogFormatter::new(theme.clone(), context.clone())
            .with_timestamps(self.show_timestamps)
            .with_targets(self.show_targets)
            .with_file_line(self.show_file_line);

        let console = FastMcpConsole::new_with_theme(theme, context);
        let rich_layer = RichLayer::new(formatter, console);

        Registry::default()
            .with(self.level_filter)
            .with(rich_layer)
    }
}
```

